## SEVERITY / VERDICT (decided HERE; apply it, do not re-argue it)
*Blocker (STOP-class where marked):* **either form, or any other failure, retried when thrown by a COMMAND, a transaction call or after a command of that attempt was sent (STOP); EF's count, cap, error list, throttling or wait formula changed, or `errorNumbersToAdd` used (STOP); either form retried inside `ExpectAnyFailure()` on the start-up read or the warm-up (STOP); EF's existing-transaction guard weakened, or a retried operation starting or committing a transaction twice (STOP);** **the CLOSE path (C3 (b)): S1 retried at head AND SqlClient can surface -2 or the pool-wait form from `Close`/`CloseAsync` AND a close runs inside a strategy operation after a write (SaveChanges or a transaction site)** = Blocker (a write can be repeated); a mark that a failure not thrown during an open or close can carry, reachable from SqlClient (C6 (c)); a path beyond the 3; a byte in an existing test file or a protected file; an assertion loosened, deleted, skipped or made conditional; `Skip`, sleep-for-timing or retry-to-green added; a build warning; a red at head not at main (3 of 3 alone); T1, T2 or T9a GREEN at main (the rows do not prove the change); names lost; a package, project, workflow, web or infra byte; an HP-tool call or data path; the head moved; a secret; a person's name, card id, `B###` token or ticket key in an added line. *Major:* the close path retried at head with SqlClient able to throw there but no write inside the operation (no repeat proven) or SqlClient's reachability left UNPROVEN either way; a reachable keyed scope nested inside a background read (C4 (a)); a survivor among P1-P3, P5, P4b, g4, g5, g7, g10, g13; g15 red; `EnableRetryOnFailure()` setting an option the new form drops that is not inert (C1 (b)); a predicted SQL Server red with a named test (C4 (c), C10) that the branch causes; an S4 concurrent pair not retried; an entry kept alive (S6); whole-suite counts that do not reconcile with base plus the named rows; a path shared with another open PR or live lane. *Minor:* the close path retried at head but PROVEN unreachable from SqlClient (then the comments `SqlServerWakeRetry.cs:38-39`, `:44-45` and the commit sentence "so no command was sent" are false text: corrected in the squash body, fix-shape for a follow-up); a false commit-message or comment sentence (text); pin gaps from g8 (if a sync Assessment read exists on a request path), g9, g11, g12; g3 survivor when a keyed request flow is reachable during a wake. *Note / Condition:* the trade-offs (dead-database error after about 90 s; abandoned-call cost; the write window of C7 (c), unless one user action writes twice); new Error-level log entries on retried reads; the same-instance rethrow during SqlClient's blocking period if harmless; the stale builder BLUF line; the unchanged `// B180:` comment line; HPSMPOC-207 not shared; unsigned commit; the builder's Sonnet trailer (replaced in the squash); the brief error of the builder kit's BUDGET table (corrected by the builder's first Correction); hosted CI, the SQL Server leg and CodeQL NOT RUN (no PR: a Condition, written in the verdict line). Say which rule you applied for every finding. **Do not pad a Note into a NO GO and do not soften a Blocker: quote the row, the plant, the source line and the number.** **VERDICT RULES.** GO needs C1-C11 measured with their controls and zero findings above Note; GO WITH FINDINGS = Minor/Note/Condition only (an open item named on the line above the last line; "NO PR; hosted CI, the SQL Server leg and CodeQL NOT RUN" is always such a Condition here); **NO GO on any Blocker or Major = NO GO round 1 of 2 on class "API retry of a connection open that timed out during a database wake"**, each finding with its fix-shape in prose (for the close path, say the shape: mark only failures raised between `ConnectionOpening` and `ConnectionOpened`, e.g. a per-connection opening flag set in `ConnectionOpening(Async)` and cleared in `ConnectionOpened(Async)`/`ConnectionClosing(Async)`, or